1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,471
The pipeline builds your Java app. Red, or green. One number decides which.

2
00:00:06,021 --> 00:00:07,787
That number is the exit code.

3
00:00:07,787 --> 00:00:10,529
A test is just a program that checks results,

4
00:00:10,529 --> 00:00:12,783
and tells the pipeline what happened.

5
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:18,176
Today you run a test that fails, read why, fix the bug, and watch it turn green.

6
00:00:18,726 --> 00:00:22,651
Then you see where the build puts its output, and why you can always delete it.

7
00:00:24,701 --> 00:00:26,600
Four facts about tests and builds.

8
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:27,409
One.

9
00:00:27,409 --> 00:00:28,705
A test is a program.

10
00:00:28,705 --> 00:00:29,872
It runs your code,

11
00:00:29,872 --> 00:00:32,399
compares the result to what you expect,

12
00:00:32,399 --> 00:00:33,955
and prints pass or fail.

13
00:00:34,505 --> 00:00:40,884
Two. A failing test exits with a non-zero code. Zero means green. Anything else means red.

14
00:00:41,434 --> 00:00:47,343
Three. A pipeline never reads your mind. It reads the exit code. Non-zero stops the build.

15
00:00:47,893 --> 00:00:48,224
Four.

16
00:00:48,224 --> 00:00:49,086
Build output,

17
00:00:49,086 --> 00:00:50,213
classes and jars,

18
00:00:50,213 --> 00:00:51,738
goes in its own folder,

19
00:00:51,738 --> 00:00:53,130
away from the source.

20
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:55,914
You can delete it and rebuild at any time.

21
00:00:56,464 --> 00:00:59,280
Source is precious. Output is disposable.

22
00:01:01,330 --> 00:01:04,317
Go to the shop folder. Type: CD, shop.

23
00:01:04,867 --> 00:01:07,856
Compile the main code into its own folder.

24
00:01:07,856 --> 00:01:08,782
Type: java C,

25
00:01:08,782 --> 00:01:09,280
dash D,

26
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:10,348
out slash main,

27
00:01:10,348 --> 00:01:11,843
then the source path.

28
00:01:12,393 --> 00:01:13,641
Compile the test,

29
00:01:13,641 --> 00:01:16,651
and tell java where the main classes are.

30
00:01:16,651 --> 00:01:17,605
Type: java C,

31
00:01:17,605 --> 00:01:18,266
dash C P,

32
00:01:18,266 --> 00:01:19,367
out slash main,

33
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:19,881
dash D,

34
00:01:19,881 --> 00:01:20,982
out slash test,

35
00:01:20,982 --> 00:01:22,377
then the test path.

36
00:01:22,927 --> 00:01:23,976
Run the test.

37
00:01:23,976 --> 00:01:24,865
Type: java,

38
00:01:24,865 --> 00:01:25,591
dash C P,

39
00:01:25,591 --> 00:01:26,803
out slash main,

40
00:01:26,803 --> 00:01:27,287
colon,

41
00:01:27,287 --> 00:01:28,498
out slash test,

42
00:01:28,498 --> 00:01:31,567
then com dot cloud cart dot cart test.

43
00:01:32,117 --> 00:01:32,674
Two pass,

44
00:01:32,674 --> 00:01:33,231
one fail.

45
00:01:33,231 --> 00:01:36,265
Ten percent off two hundred should be one eighty.

46
00:01:36,265 --> 00:01:37,813
The code returned twenty.

47
00:01:38,363 --> 00:01:42,373
Now the exit code. Type: echo, dollar sign, question mark.

48
00:01:42,923 --> 00:01:46,123
One. Not zero. This is what a pipeline sees. Red.

49
00:01:46,673 --> 00:01:49,150
The bug: the discount function returns the discount,

50
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,246
not the price after it.

51
00:01:50,246 --> 00:01:51,008
Fix it with sed.

52
00:01:51,008 --> 00:01:51,484
Type: sed,

53
00:01:51,484 --> 00:01:51,817
dash I,

54
00:01:51,817 --> 00:01:52,103
quote,

55
00:01:52,103 --> 00:01:52,198
s,

56
00:01:52,198 --> 00:01:52,437
pipe,

57
00:01:52,437 --> 00:01:53,199
total slash ten,

58
00:01:53,199 --> 00:01:53,437
pipe,

59
00:01:53,437 --> 00:01:54,770
total minus total slash ten,

60
00:01:54,770 --> 00:01:55,009
pipe,

61
00:01:55,009 --> 00:01:55,294
quote,

62
00:01:55,294 --> 00:01:56,295
then the source path.

63
00:01:56,845 --> 00:02:02,327
Rebuild the main code. Type: java C, dash D, out slash main, then the source path.

64
00:02:02,877 --> 00:02:04,373
Run the test again.

65
00:02:04,373 --> 00:02:05,239
Type: java,

66
00:02:05,239 --> 00:02:05,948
dash C P,

67
00:02:05,948 --> 00:02:07,129
out slash main,

68
00:02:07,129 --> 00:02:07,601
colon,

69
00:02:07,601 --> 00:02:08,782
out slash test,

70
00:02:08,782 --> 00:02:11,773
then com dot cloud cart dot cart test.

71
00:02:12,323 --> 00:02:14,606
Three pass, zero failed. Green.

72
00:02:15,156 --> 00:02:19,039
And the exit code. Type: echo, dollar sign, question mark.

73
00:02:19,589 --> 00:02:22,127
Zero. Green. The pipeline moves on.

74
00:02:24,177 --> 00:02:27,164
Go to the shop folder. Type: CD, shop.

75
00:02:27,714 --> 00:02:33,068
Build the main code. Type: java C, dash D, out slash main, then the source path.

76
00:02:33,618 --> 00:02:34,747
Build the test.

77
00:02:34,747 --> 00:02:35,725
Type: java C,

78
00:02:35,725 --> 00:02:36,402
dash C P,

79
00:02:36,402 --> 00:02:37,531
out slash main,

80
00:02:37,531 --> 00:02:38,058
dash D,

81
00:02:38,058 --> 00:02:39,186
out slash test,

82
00:02:39,186 --> 00:02:40,616
then the test path.

83
00:02:41,166 --> 00:02:45,646
Where did the output go? Type: find, out, dash type, f, pipe, sort.

84
00:02:46,196 --> 00:02:47,260
Two class files,

85
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:48,924
in two folders under out.

86
00:02:48,924 --> 00:02:50,853
Main and test are kept apart.

87
00:02:50,853 --> 00:02:52,916
The source folder is untouched.

88
00:02:53,466 --> 00:02:55,864
Package the main classes only.

89
00:02:55,864 --> 00:02:56,663
Type: jar,

90
00:02:56,663 --> 00:02:56,983
C F,

91
00:02:56,983 --> 00:02:58,502
cloud cart dot jar,

92
00:02:58,502 --> 00:02:59,062
dash C,

93
00:02:59,062 --> 00:03:00,261
out slash main,

94
00:03:00,261 --> 00:03:00,741
space,

95
00:03:00,741 --> 00:03:01,060
dot.

96
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:05,493
Look inside. Type: jar, T F, cloud cart dot jar.

97
00:03:06,043 --> 00:03:10,288
The cart class is in. The test is not. You ship the code, not its tests.

98
00:03:10,838 --> 00:03:16,044
Now throw the build away. Type: R M, dash R, out, cloud cart dot jar.

99
00:03:16,594 --> 00:03:18,663
List the folder. Type: L S.

100
00:03:19,213 --> 00:03:20,726
Only the source is left.

101
00:03:20,726 --> 00:03:22,743
One command rebuilds everything.

102
00:03:22,743 --> 00:03:24,886
That is why you never edit output,

103
00:03:24,886 --> 00:03:26,146
and never commit it.

104
00:03:28,196 --> 00:03:29,924
Reading a build, in this order.

105
00:03:30,474 --> 00:03:34,357
First, the exit code. Zero is green. Anything else is red.

106
00:03:34,907 --> 00:03:39,685
Second, the test output. Which test failed, what was expected, what was returned.

107
00:03:40,235 --> 00:03:40,634
Third,

108
00:03:40,634 --> 00:03:41,832
the output folder.

109
00:03:41,832 --> 00:03:42,364
Classes,

110
00:03:42,364 --> 00:03:42,697
jars,

111
00:03:42,697 --> 00:03:44,227
and reports live there.

112
00:03:44,227 --> 00:03:46,422
Delete and rebuild when in doubt.

113
00:03:46,972 --> 00:03:50,193
Red tells you something is wrong. The output tells you what.

114
00:03:52,243 --> 00:03:53,119
Your lab task.

115
00:03:53,119 --> 00:03:56,184
Lab eighty-two gives you a cart class with a bug,

116
00:03:56,184 --> 00:03:56,997
and its test.

117
00:03:56,997 --> 00:03:58,686
Lab check judges your work.

118
00:03:59,236 --> 00:04:01,367
It lives at git hub dot com,

119
00:04:01,367 --> 00:04:02,890
slash it dash waves,

120
00:04:02,890 --> 00:04:04,641
slash dev ops dash A I,

121
00:04:04,641 --> 00:04:05,479
in academy,

122
00:04:05,479 --> 00:04:05,783
lab,

123
00:04:05,783 --> 00:04:07,534
lab eighty-two dot S H.

124
00:04:08,084 --> 00:04:12,650
One: compile main into out slash main, and the test into out slash test.

125
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,805
Two: run the test before fixing anything,

126
00:04:15,805 --> 00:04:19,045
and save the output into test dash before dot text.

127
00:04:19,595 --> 00:04:22,816
Three: fix the bug in cart dot java, and rebuild.

128
00:04:23,366 --> 00:04:26,918
Four: run the test again into test dash after dot text,

129
00:04:26,918 --> 00:04:30,470
and pack only the main classes into cloud cart dot jar.

130
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,766
Five: answers dot text,

131
00:04:32,766 --> 00:04:33,676
three lines.

132
00:04:33,676 --> 00:04:36,257
A failed test exits with non-zero.

133
00:04:36,257 --> 00:04:38,609
The build output folder is out.

134
00:04:38,609 --> 00:04:40,962
The jar holds compiled classes.

135
00:04:41,512 --> 00:04:42,043
Install,

136
00:04:42,043 --> 00:04:42,840
then lab up,

137
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:43,504
lab check,

138
00:04:43,504 --> 00:04:44,368
and lab down,

139
00:04:44,368 --> 00:04:45,165
like before.

140
00:04:45,165 --> 00:04:47,954
The shortcut file is shortcuts eighty-two.

141
00:04:50,004 --> 00:04:52,073
Pass or fail. You need all six.

142
00:04:52,623 --> 00:04:54,437
Five pass lines in lab check.

143
00:04:54,987 --> 00:04:56,501
You can say what a test is.

144
00:04:57,051 --> 00:04:58,630
You can read a failing test.

145
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:00,908
You can explain exit codes.

146
00:05:01,458 --> 00:05:03,506
You can find and rebuild the output.

147
00:05:04,056 --> 00:05:05,976
lab down, nothing left behind.

148
00:05:06,526 --> 00:05:07,827
To pass, all six.

149
00:05:09,877 --> 00:05:12,714
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

150
00:05:13,264 --> 00:05:15,355
One: lab up, and read the task file.

151
00:05:15,905 --> 00:05:19,297
Two: compile, run the test, and save the failing result.

152
00:05:19,847 --> 00:05:21,788
Three: fix the bug, and rebuild.

153
00:05:22,338 --> 00:05:24,877
Four: run the test again, and build the jar.

154
00:05:25,427 --> 00:05:27,710
Five: write your answers, and lab check.

155
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:30,841
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

